{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-98ec296eceb0b42b", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# UniMoE-Audio: Unified Speech and Music Generation with Dynamic-Capacity MoE\narXiv: 2510.13344\nAuthors: Zhenyu Liu, Yunxin Li, Xuanyu Zhang, Qixun Teng, Shenyuan Jiang, Xinyu Chen, Haoyuan Shi, Jinchao Li, Qi Wang, Haolan Chen, Fanbo Meng, Mingjun Zhao, Yu Xu, Yancheng He, Baotian Hu, Min Zhang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose UniMoE-Audio, a unified speech and music generation model based on a novel Dynamic-Capacity MoE framework that integrates a Top-P routing strategy and a hybrid expert design to mitigate inherent task conflict.\n  2. We introduce a data-aware, three-stage training curriculum that systematically overcomes data imbalance through independent specialist training, router warmup, and synergistic joint training.\n  3. We provide extensive experiments demonstrating that UniMoE-Audio achieves state-of-the-art or competitive performance on major speech and music generation benchmarks while revealing valuable insights into the dynamic activation patterns of the unified MoE model.\n\nTags: TTS", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "99f9f2f5-463f-4d73-8c1b-6ee352cfb6b2", "uuid": "009946d3-1181-4fd6-aaab-28826490e553", "timestamp": "2026-08-11T14:47:50.562Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# UniMoE-Audio: Unified Speech and Music Generation with Dynamic-Capacity MoE\narXiv: 2510.13344\nAuthors: Zhenyu Liu, Yunxin Li, Xuanyu Zhang, Qixun Teng, Shenyuan Jiang, Xinyu Chen, Haoyuan Shi, Jinchao Li, Qi Wang, Haolan Chen, Fanbo Meng, Mingjun Zhao, Yu Xu, Yancheng He, Baotian Hu, Min Zhang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose UniMoE-Audio, a unified speech and music generation model based on a novel Dynamic-Capacity MoE framework that integrates a Top-P routing strategy and a hybrid expert design to mitigate inherent task conflict.\n  2. We introduce a data-aware, three-stage training curriculum that systematically overcomes data imbalance through independent specialist training, router warmup, and synergistic joint training.\n  3. We provide extensive experiments demonstrating that UniMoE-Audio achieves state-of-the-art or competitive performance on major speech and music generation benchmarks while revealing valuable insights into the dynamic activation patterns of the unified MoE model.\n\nTags: TTS", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b9a1f671e203c68c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Dasheng AudioGen: A Unified Model for Generating Coherent Audio Scenes from Text\narXiv: 2605.27838\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Dasheng AudioGen, a unified text-to-audio framework that jointly generates intelligible speech, music, sound effects, and environmental acoustics within a single audio scene without domain-specific modeling.\n  2. We introduce structured multi-view captions, a layered design that provides fine-grained supervision and disentangled control over different audio components while remaining compatible with agentic systems.\n  3. We introduce a unified semantic-acoustic representation based on DashengTokenizer as the shared latent space, which provides semantic priors for efficient training and sufficient capacity to disentangle and fuse concurrent audio components.\n  4. We establish a comprehensive evaluation pipeline for audio scene generation, demonstrating that Dasheng AudioGen substantially outperforms expert pipelines in mixed-audio scenes while remaining competitive with specialized models.\n\nTags: method, experiments, we propose, we introduce", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "99f9f2f5-463f-4d73-8c1b-6ee352cfb6b2", "uuid": "d68c5745-84de-434c-9cff-ad93937f4332", "timestamp": "2026-08-11T14:47:50.960Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Dasheng AudioGen: A Unified Model for Generating Coherent Audio Scenes from Text\narXiv: 2605.27838\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Dasheng AudioGen, a unified text-to-audio framework that jointly generates intelligible speech, music, sound effects, and environmental acoustics within a single audio scene without domain-specific modeling.\n  2. We introduce structured multi-view captions, a layered design that provides fine-grained supervision and disentangled control over different audio components while remaining compatible with agentic systems.\n  3. We introduce a unified semantic-acoustic representation based on DashengTokenizer as the shared latent space, which provides semantic priors for efficient training and sufficient capacity to disentangle and fuse concurrent audio components.\n  4. We establish a comprehensive evaluation pipeline for audio scene generation, demonstrating that Dasheng AudioGen substantially outperforms expert pipelines in mixed-audio scenes while remaining competitive with specialized models.\n\nTags: method, experiments, we propose, we introduce", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
